# The shape a message-only extent misses. Two transformers whose message
# blocks are disjoint and whose bodies interleave: the second's entire body
# sits inside the first's span, because the first's challenge follows all of
# it.
#
# The derivation succeeds, and should: a round-by-round bound reaches a
# protocol by a union bound over its rounds, every challenge here stays fresh
# given the prefix the duplex absorbed, and the judgment is a true statement
# about the transformer it prices. What the artifact judgment refuses is the
# step from that to a statement about the artifact, and it refuses it by
# naming the round nobody indexed.
#
# The gate this replaces admitted this artifact outright, and priced one of
# the two bodies with nothing said about the other.
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: zkc-seal %S/Inputs/body-interleaved-open.mlir %zkc-seal-full -o %t/sealed.artifacts > /dev/null
# RUN: %python %S/../SemanticClosure/lib/artifact_handoff.py stage %t/sealed.artifacts %t/sealed.mlirbc
# RUN: zkc-derive --signature=%zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json \
# RUN:   --protocol-vocabulary=%zkc-registry-dir/protocol-vocabulary.json \
# RUN:   --construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json \
# RUN:   --request=%S/Inputs/body-interleaved-request.json -o=/dev/null %t/sealed.mlirbc \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: artifact judgment: not discharged
# CHECK: belongs to no transformer this derivation covers
